module System/Memory

### One user at a time: `modifying g` waits until no other agent has `g` open, and it is used to read as well (an
### `Exclusive` `Guarded` has no `viewing`). The state is one byte, and the runtime's AccessManager keeps who holds
### it: an agent that has to wait goes through the AccessManager, which stops the program when agents wait on each
### other (`[debug] deadlock-check`).
### :see: {AccessPolicy}, {MultiRead}, {Guarded}
record Exclusive
obeys AccessPolicy
    ### The byte whose access the AccessManager hands out: its address names this access.
    secret guard: U8

### Creates a free exclusive access.
### :returns: The resulting `Exclusive` value.
routine Exclusive() -> Exclusive
    return Exclusive(guard: 0)

### The AccessManager's kind for this policy: an exclusive access.
### :returns: 1.
@readonly
routine Exclusive.access_kind() -> U32
    return 1
